  <!-- TIE CARD SECTION -->
  <div class="msv__section">
    <div class="msv__container--narrow">
      <h2>The TIE Card: Your Foreigner ID</h2>
      <p>Once your residence permit is approved, you must apply for a TIE (Tarjeta de Identidad de Extranjero), Spain's official foreigner identification card. The TIE is your primary document for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Opening bank accounts and conducting financial transactions</li>
        <li>Employment and tax registration (obtaining an NIE if you don't have one)</li>
        <li>Renting property and signing contracts</li>
        <li>Healthcare and social services</li>
        <li>Official identification throughout Spain</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Learn more about TIE card requirements, timelines, and the application process in our <a href="/tie-card-spain.html">complete TIE card guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- RENEWAL SECTION -->
