      <h2>Residence Permit Renewal</h2>
      <p>Most residence permits are renewable, but timing and requirements vary by type:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Temporary permits:</strong> Valid for 1 year; renewal applications should be submitted 60 days before expiry.</li>
        <li><strong>Permanent permits:</strong> Valid indefinitely but require renewal documentation every 5 years; renewal is usually straightforward if you've maintained legal residency.</li>
        <li><strong>EU Long-Term permits:</strong> Valid for 5 years; renewal requires proof of continuous legal residence and compliance with Spanish law.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Timely renewal ensures continuous legal status and avoids gaps that could affect your work authorization or access to services. Plan ahead and begin the process early. For detailed renewal guidance, see our <a href="/spanish-residency-renewal.html">residence permit renewal guide</a>.</p>
